        /// </tr>
        /// <tr>
        /// <td><c>DISABLED</c></td>
        /// <td>Synchronization is disabled. Existing configurations, credentials, and users are retained.</td>
        /// <td>To re-establish access, check and prepare the receiving end first, and then enable synchronization.</td>
        /// </tr>
        /// <tr>
        /// <td><c>UPDATE_FAILED</c></td>
        /// <td>The operation failed, or the configuration and credentials after enabling are no longer available.</td>
        /// <td>Check the operation results and access configuration in combination with <c>operationStatus</c>.</td>
        /// </tr>
        /// <tr>
        /// <td>This operation queries the SCIM status. The SAML enterprise account logon configuration is queried through <a href="https://api.aliyun.com/document/AgentCore/2026-08-04/GetIdentityProvider">GetIdentityProvider</a>. <c>READY</c> reflects the result of the current enabling operation. The user assignment and provisioning status in the enterprise identity system must still be verified on the enterprise side.</td>
